# Caddy in front of the account service (docker-compose.yml here runs it).
#
# MR_AUTH_SITE lists the sites Caddy serves: the issuer's own origin first, then its two check
# names where the profile has them. `http://localhost:4455` serves plain HTTP on port 4455
# (local-dev), and an `https://` name gets an ACME certificate on ports 80 and 443 (hosted-dev,
# production), kept in the /data volume. Caddy serves no other host name. MR_AUTH_UPSTREAM is the
# profile's account service.
#
# The proxy passes the client's Host unchanged; the service answers only its issuer's host and,
# for POST /world/check, the two check names, and takes the scheme from its issuer. It reads one
# thing a proxy says: the last address in X-Forwarded-For, from a proxy inside
# MR_ACCOUNT_TRUSTED_PROXY, as the request's source address. So that header is written here as
# the one address Caddy itself takes the request to come from, whatever a client sent in it.
{$MR_AUTH_SITE} {
	reverse_proxy {$MR_AUTH_UPSTREAM} {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For {client_ip}
	}
}
